<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aflah ibn Abd al-Wahhab</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 823–872</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aflah ibn Abd al-Wahhab was the third <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imam</a> of the Rustamid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imamate">Imamate</a>, the Ibadi state centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiaret">Tahert</a> in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a>, ruling for about fifty years in the 9th century. His long reign is remembered as the high point of the dynasty, when Tahert prospered from Saharan caravan trade and was known for its learned and open religious debate.</p></div>
